comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T17:08:40.427Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-10-02: complete strict all-status corpus read returned 2851/2851 items with no omissions or unreadable files; exact GitHub issue/ID and contract-title searches found no canonical owner for this residual acceptance. Existing foundations are linked, including closed historical work; no closed fix is asserted outstanding. Imported report and acceptance are planning evidence, not current reproduction or implementation completion. This item remains open and unclaimed until selected for implementation."
body: "## Outcome\nMake project management = context management operationally testable: an agent receives the smallest authorized, current, evidence-complete working set, makes the right next decision, and resumes interrupted work without repeating effects.\n\nThis is a planning umbrella. No implementation or new defect reproduction is claimed. Public SDK primitives own semantics; CLI, MCP and package adapters stay thin.\n\n## Existing foundations to reuse\n- [Adaptive context engine pm-4k6b](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-4k6b.toon), [context evaluation pm-atfm](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-atfm.toon), and [caller-carried output sessions pm-hid9g1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-hid9g1.toon)\n- Complete-result and omission contracts in #947 and #1035; exact delivery feedback and source fingerprints in #1176\n- Temporal replay/domain exemplar in #656; existing schema/custom fields, evidence, history and typed supersedes relationships\n- Existing claims, Plans, handoff/context and durable MCP task mechanisms; [concurrency pm-dj98](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/epics/pm-dj98.toon) and [fleet outcome pm-z1kr34](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/milestones/pm-z1kr34.toon)\n- #863 already delivers tokens-per-completed-task accounting. Extend its decision coverage rather than building a second meter\n- #1336 remains an open report with canonical [stale-claim owner pm-szv11n](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/stories/pm-szv11n.toon). #1337 is still open, but merged #1341 already fixes stripped preview retries; preserve that fix and do not refile it as a current reproduced bug\n\n## Delivery workstreams\n1. #1358 — Typed temporal knowledge reconciliation and dependency invalidation\n2. #1361 — Cross-provider semantic context coverage and coherent read receipts\n3. #1359 — Durable execution checkpoints with claim-generation fencing\n4. #1360 — Separate knowledge identity, visibility and action authority; scope-before-ranking and effect-preserving recovery\n5. #1362 — Decision-level scenario evaluation and success-per-token gates\n\n## Lightweight-default design constraint\n\nAll workstreams must follow #1363: keep the generic core lightweight, make advanced capabilities opt-in, and expose additional information through truthful progressive discovery. Required constraints, blockers, authority boundaries and insufficient-context outcomes must remain visible at the decision point. Git, coding, tests, claims and richer context/execution contracts must not become unconditional prerequisites for a simple task.\n\n#1363 documents the capability-policy and migration plan, capability-aware guidance/help, and a six-task × two-approach × three-run total-agent-effort comparison extending #1362 and existing token accounting. Its reproduced baseline observations are distinguished from proposed implementation. The five children above remain planning work.\n\n## Implementation sequence\n1. Inventory the actual SDK exports, provider contracts and canonical PM owners at implementation time. Reuse existing owners for shipped/overlapping slices; only assign residual acceptance work.\n2. Agree versioned knowledge, coverage, checkpoint and policy contracts together. Names suggested in children are illustrative, not promised APIs.\n3. Implement pure deterministic SDK kernels, then storage/provider integration and thin CLI/MCP adapters. Capture dependency fingerprints before optimizing incremental reads.\n4. Define scenario fixtures and negative controls at the outset. Wire each workstream's executable acceptance into the existing eval/assurance pipeline.\n5. Verify packed Node/Bun SDK consumers and CLI/MCP parity; document migration, recovery and explicit consistency limits.\n\n## Cross-cutting acceptance\n- [ ] All five workstreams have named residual scope, linked existing ownership, tests and implementation documentation\n- [ ] Existing schemas remain readable; no silent promotion of old prose to verified truth, granted authority, or completed execution\n- [ ] Mandatory context omissions produce an explicit insufficient-context outcome; token savings cannot conceal lost decision evidence\n- [ ] Authorization precedes provider access/ranking; identity, visibility and action permission remain independent\n- [ ] Resume either verifies prior effects or returns an explicit unknown/blocked state; stale owners cannot commit after takeover\n- [ ] Decision correctness, abstention, effect safety, actual delivered token cost and latency are measured together\n- [ ] Existing quality/security/coverage/token ratchets remain intact; new gates include executable negative controls and non-vacuous denominators\n\n## Non-goals\nNo replacement project-management database, parallel session-budget ledger, separate retrieval harness, new identity provider, mandatory central server, automatic truth resolution from recency alone, or promise of exactly-once external effects.\n\n## Deduplication evidence\nReviewed open and closed GitHub issue/PR search results and public canonical PM records on 2026-09-30. Existing umbrella programs cover broad goals; these children are bounded implementation slices for the additional contracts and their acceptance evidence. If implementation-time inventory proves a slice already complete, attach exact evidence and narrow or close that slice rather than implementing it again."
